# Milestone: M3
# Covers: Lobby is an alias for the global Realm; bindings in Lobby are visible
#         globally and vice versa.
#
# blocked: Lobby proto is UPROTO_READONLY; Lobby.x = v raises TypeError — v1.0-rc investigation
# matrix-row: stdlib-lobby
#
# Reason: Lobby is a stdlib concept — a reflective surface that exposes the
# global Realm as an object. The Lobby binding lands at M6 (stdlib) when the
# standard library is bootstrapped. At M3, Realm is a C-level type only,
# not exposed as an urbiscript binding.
#
# When M6 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the urbiscript source.
# Expected behaviour: Lobby is the global Realm; setting Lobby.x sets a global
# binding visible to all subsequent code.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M6):
#   Lobby.x = 123;
#   x
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 123
